\begin{problem}
Find the : sum of the digits of the base-8 expression for $8888_{10}$.
\end{problem}
To find the base-8 expression for $8888_{10}$, we repeatedly divide by 8 and keep track of the remainders.
\begin{itemize}
    \item $8888 \div 8 = 1111$ with a remainder of $0$.
    \item $1111 \div 8 = 138$ with a remainder of $7$.
    \item $138 \div 8 = 17$ with a remainder of $2$.
    \item $17 \div 8 = 2$ with a remainder of $1$.
    \item $2 \div 8 = 0$ with a remainder of $2$.
\end{itemize}
Reading the remainders in reverse order gives us $21270_8$.
The digits in the base-8 expression are $2, 1, 2, 7, 0$. The sum of the digits is $2+1+2+7+0 = 12$.

Alternatively, we can convert $8888_{10}$ to base 8.
\begin{align*} 8888 \div 8 &= 1111 \text{ remainder } 0 \\ 1111 \div 8 &= 138 \text{ remainder } 7 \\ 138 \div 8 &= 17 \text{ remainder } 2 \\ 17 \div 8 &= 2 \text{ remainder } 1 \\ 2 \div 8 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 2 \end{align*}
Reading the remainders in reverse order, we get $21270_8$. The sum of the digits is $2+1+2+7+0=12$.
\end{answer}
\boxed{12}

